WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.429 --> 00:00:04.580
Caped crusaders and awesome avengers are everywhere
you look at the movies, and there's a great

00:00:04.580 --> 00:00:08.420
selection of crowd-pleasing blockbusters that
take the format to new heights.

00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:14.160
From '70s classics to modern-day epics, these
are the 30 best superhero movies ever made.

00:00:14.780 --> 00:00:19.840
This 2010 film based on the comic series of
the same name isn't your typical superhero

00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:22.680
story, and that's exactly what makes it so
great.

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:27.140
It's the story of a kid who really has no
business being a hero but does it anyway,

00:00:27.140 --> 00:00:30.279
with bone-cracking, profane, with over-the-top
action.

00:00:30.279 --> 00:00:35.070
Kick-Ass proved to be a breakout project for
Aaron Johnson and Chloë Grace Moretz, and

00:00:35.070 --> 00:00:38.960
when veteran weirdo Nicolas Cage is involved,
how can you possibly go wrong?

00:00:47.020 --> 00:00:47.820
Never mind.

00:00:47.980 --> 00:00:49.140
Kick-Ass is great, though.

00:00:49.760 --> 00:00:54.120
Chronicle gives the superhero genre the found
footage treatment, telling the story of three

00:00:54.129 --> 00:01:00.129
teenagers who stumble upon a mysterious extraterrestrial
object that grants them seemingly limitless

00:01:00.129 --> 00:01:00.700
superpowers.

00:01:01.060 --> 00:01:04.960
Of course, being a teen is hard enough, but
being a teen with telekinesis?

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:09.900
Well, that's too much of a burden to bear,
and this superhero origin story quickly turns

00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:10.440
evil.

00:01:10.780 --> 00:01:14.200
A surprise hit, the movie resonated with critics
and fans alike.

00:01:14.380 --> 00:01:18.280
Sure, there are moments when you'll wonder
why the cameras are still rolling as psychic

00:01:18.290 --> 00:01:22.290
high school students battle it out in the
sky, but the movie is such a tense thrill

00:01:22.290 --> 00:01:26.520
ride that you'll quickly forget any flaws
as the movie heads towards its inevitable

00:01:26.520 --> 00:01:27.900
and horrific showdown.

00:01:28.580 --> 00:01:33.680
Big Hero 6 is a loose adaptation of a quirky,
obscure Marvel comic, and was one of the best

00:01:33.680 --> 00:01:37.840
films of 2014, animated, superhero, or otherwise.

00:01:38.170 --> 00:01:42.520
It follows a kid whose brother is tragically
killed in a fire, and how he moves on from

00:01:42.520 --> 00:01:46.700
that loss by making friends with his brother's
robot and the friends he left behind.

00:01:47.360 --> 00:01:50.950
When they realize there must have been more
to the fire than it seemed, they suit up as

00:01:50.950 --> 00:01:55.900
superheroes to get justice, but not even the
film's villain is as cut and dried as it might

00:01:55.900 --> 00:01:56.440
appear.

00:01:56.780 --> 00:02:01.060
The visuals are great, the tone is pitch perfect,
and there's even a Stan Lee cameo.

00:02:01.820 --> 00:02:06.579
Liam Neeson has a special set of skills, and
that usually includes playing dudes you just

00:02:06.580 --> 00:02:07.400
don't mess with.

00:02:11.140 --> 00:02:12.440
"I see you when you're sleeping.

00:02:13.860 --> 00:02:15.340
I know when you're awake."

00:02:16.240 --> 00:02:20.940
But before he fought human traffickers, wolves,
and LEGO lawbreakers, he was Darkman.

00:02:21.320 --> 00:02:26.660
This flick finds Neeson playing Peyton Westlake,
a scientist who becomes a scarred and reluctant

00:02:26.660 --> 00:02:27.160
superhero.

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:32.160
Beneath the layers of monster makeup, Neeson
strikes the perfect balance of madness, righteous

00:02:32.160 --> 00:02:33.240
anger, and pathos.

00:02:33.540 --> 00:02:39.400
Notable for its bizarre rage sequences, clever
practical effects, and campy tone, this 1990

00:02:39.400 --> 00:02:43.520
flick feels a mash-up of Batman, Evil Dead
II, and The Phantom of the Opera.

00:02:43.969 --> 00:02:48.720
If you're tired of the usual Marvel and DC
fare, this film goes to weird and wacky places

00:02:48.720 --> 00:02:51.060
most superhero movies would never dare.

00:02:51.800 --> 00:02:57.480
Hellboy is a 2004 film which follows the titular
half-demon, memorably played by Ron Perlman,

00:02:57.480 --> 00:03:00.280
as he helps humanity take on supernatural
threats.

00:03:00.500 --> 00:03:05.280
Director Guillermo Del Toro's visual style
is perfectly suited to this story, which follows

00:03:05.290 --> 00:03:10.230
Hellboy as he tries to figure out just exactly
what he is, while also battling all sorts

00:03:10.230 --> 00:03:11.540
of baddies along the way.

00:03:11.890 --> 00:03:16.340
The effects work is out of this world, and
the design of villains like the undead, clockwork

00:03:16.340 --> 00:03:18.080
Kroenen is totally terrifying.

00:03:18.740 --> 00:03:23.980
It takes a special kind of magic to get Hellboy
right, but del Toro and Perlman possess exactly

00:03:23.980 --> 00:03:26.540
what it takes to give us a devilishly good
movie.

00:03:26.900 --> 00:03:31.440
It's an absolute miracle this blood-soaked,
F-bomb drenched movie ever made it onto the

00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:33.980
big screen, but aren't we all glad it did?

00:03:34.120 --> 00:03:38.440
Deadpool lived in development hell for years,
and it took the leak of a concept reel to

00:03:38.440 --> 00:03:39.760
finally jumpstart it.

00:03:39.940 --> 00:03:43.700
The results are quick, filthy and fun, with
Ryan Reynolds born to play the part.

00:03:43.960 --> 00:03:48.159
The Merc With A Mouth now holds the record
for the highest-grossing X-Men film and the

00:03:48.160 --> 00:03:49.900
highest-grossing R-rated film in history.

00:03:50.840 --> 00:03:55.440
A magnificent conflict between Sir Patrick
Stewart's Professor X and Sir Ian McKellan's

00:03:55.450 --> 00:04:01.799
Magneto, 2003's X2: X-Men United is considered
by many to be the best of the original X-Men

00:04:01.800 --> 00:04:04.540
trilogy, and it just couldn't be made today.

00:04:04.940 --> 00:04:09.900
That energy and fierceness has dispersed from
popular imagination, replaced by the cynicism

00:04:09.900 --> 00:04:12.560
of Deadpool and the grim pessimism of Logan.

00:04:12.980 --> 00:04:17.760
Doing justice to its source material, the
1982 masterpiece God Loves, Man Kills, this

00:04:17.800 --> 00:04:19.120
film is required viewing.

00:04:20.040 --> 00:04:25.380
With 1989's Batman, director Tim Burton managed
to take a character best known for Adam West's

00:04:25.380 --> 00:04:29.520
goofiness and turn him into a serious hero
for comic book fans.

00:04:29.900 --> 00:04:34.560
With the franchise's staying power fading
fast in the late 1970s, it took more than

00:04:34.560 --> 00:04:37.400
a decade to finally get a new adaptation mounted.

00:04:37.640 --> 00:04:42.520
Many fans flew into an uproar over Michael
Keaton's casting in the title role, but one

00:04:42.520 --> 00:04:45.240
look at the final film made all those worries
melt away.

00:04:45.740 --> 00:04:49.939
Burton treated the canon seriously, and though
he didn't follow it note for note, he paid

00:04:49.940 --> 00:04:53.400
tribute to it and built a living, breathing
version of Gotham City.

00:04:54.060 --> 00:04:58.400
Combining the worlds of the original X-Men
trilogy with the X-Men prequel-sequel series

00:04:58.409 --> 00:05:03.120
was a tall order, but Bryan Singer pulled
it off with his return to the franchise after

00:05:03.120 --> 00:05:04.820
taking a break for a couple of films.

00:05:05.340 --> 00:05:10.380
Days of Future Past managed to weave together
a story spanning decades, with two separate

00:05:10.380 --> 00:05:14.090
casts, and still keep all the story tight
enough so even someone who's never seen an

00:05:14.090 --> 00:05:15.860
X-Men film could follow along.

00:05:16.410 --> 00:05:21.700
It also stealthily retconned out the atrocious
X-Men: The Last Stand, making all things right

00:05:21.720 --> 00:05:23.520
within the cinematic X-universe.

00:05:24.200 --> 00:05:28.451
Batman Returns is less about Batman than it
is about the creation of Catwoman, played

00:05:28.460 --> 00:05:30.180
outstandingly by Michelle Pfeiffer.

00:05:38.380 --> 00:05:38.880
"Meow."

00:05:39.320 --> 00:05:43.780
It also happens to feature Michael Keaton
returning to his role as Batman, and Danny

00:05:43.780 --> 00:05:48.160
DeVito as a hideous version of the Penguin,
in a part written specifically for him.

00:05:48.669 --> 00:05:52.919
With Pfeiffer in the catsuit, Tim Burton at
the height of his directorial powers, and

00:05:52.919 --> 00:05:57.860
Keaton's willingness to let his smug yet charming
Bruce Wayne share the spotlight with two formidable

00:05:57.860 --> 00:06:02.320
foes, this sequel earned praise from critics
and became a box office hit.

00:06:03.040 --> 00:06:08.060
"The liberation of Gotham has begun."

00:06:11.320 --> 00:06:16.819
In 2019, the DC Extended Universe saw Ben
Affleck hang up the Bat-cape, and Henry Cavill's

00:06:16.820 --> 00:06:18.680
Superman was still up in the air.

00:06:18.840 --> 00:06:23.680
Even the runaway success of Aquaman couldn't
seem to save Warner Bros.' superhero franchise.

00:06:23.940 --> 00:06:26.900
That's when Shazam! arrived to electrify audiences.

00:06:27.100 --> 00:06:32.080
Shazam! tells the tale of Billy Batson, a
kid who's granted Superman-like superpowers,

00:06:32.080 --> 00:06:35.060
and the ability to transform into an adult,
by an aging wizard.

00:06:35.520 --> 00:06:39.740
The result is a movie that strips away all
the DC darkness and gives us a film that's

00:06:39.740 --> 00:06:41.340
both sweet and fun.

00:06:41.760 --> 00:06:45.400
It's also a movie about the importance of
family and finding your place in the world,

00:06:45.600 --> 00:06:49.380
which is a lot nicer than watching the Caped
Crusader murdering people.

00:06:49.740 --> 00:06:53.590
On top of all that, Shazam! has the right
amount of weirdness to make it stand out from

00:06:53.590 --> 00:06:54.640
the superhero pack.

00:06:55.000 --> 00:06:59.580
It isn't afraid to embrace its oddball comic
book origins, and the result is an absolute

00:06:59.580 --> 00:07:00.080
blast.

00:07:00.340 --> 00:07:04.180
And ultimately, that's kind of the point of
the film: It's really fun to be a superhero.

00:07:04.980 --> 00:07:09.860
Guardians of the Galaxy earns its spot by
being a galactic joy to behold, bringing '70s

00:07:09.860 --> 00:07:12.780
arena rock and Marvel superheroes to outer
space.

00:07:13.160 --> 00:07:17.820
Zoe Saldana enchants as the green-skinned
Gamora; Bradley Cooper shows his impressive

00:07:17.820 --> 00:07:22.289
range as the voice of Rocket Raccoon, and
Vin Diesel's Groot makes three words speak

00:07:22.289 --> 00:07:23.120
volumes.

00:07:23.289 --> 00:07:26.699
Plus, Dave Bautista's Drax the Destroyer steals
every scene.

00:07:26.699 --> 00:07:28.650
"Nothing goes over my head.

00:07:28.650 --> 00:07:30.530
My reflexes are too fast.

00:07:30.530 --> 00:07:31.900
I would catch it."

00:07:32.080 --> 00:07:35.640
Before Guardians, the Marvel Cinematic Universe
had been pretty straightforward.

00:07:35.940 --> 00:07:40.439
Sure, there were fire-breathing dudes, and
dark elves, but this was a movie about a talking

00:07:40.440 --> 00:07:43.660
tree, a smart-aleck raccoon, and a whistling
space pirate.

00:07:43.820 --> 00:07:47.980
Writer-director James Gunn pulled it off,
injecting those losers and scoundrels with

00:07:47.990 --> 00:07:49.259
wit and warmth.

00:07:49.260 --> 00:07:50.460
We are all Groot.

00:07:51.100 --> 00:07:55.940
In 1995, Sylvester Stallone tried bringing
Judge Dredd to the silver screen, and the

00:07:55.940 --> 00:07:57.700
result was an absolute disaster.

00:07:58.340 --> 00:07:59.200
"You started a massacre!"

00:07:59.420 --> 00:08:00.420
"I caused a revolution!"

00:08:00.440 --> 00:08:01.460
"You betrayed the law!"

00:08:01.560 --> 00:08:02.760
"LAAAAAAAAWWWW!!!"

00:08:03.200 --> 00:08:07.840
Fortunately, the mean-mugging lawman got a
second shot in 2012, when Karl Urban donned

00:08:07.840 --> 00:08:08.880
the grungy red helmet.

00:08:09.490 --> 00:08:14.100
The plot of Dredd is incredibly simple: the
world is a dystopian nightmare, and Mega-City

00:08:14.110 --> 00:08:18.319
One is crawling with crime, and Dredd and
his psychic partner have to clear out floor

00:08:18.320 --> 00:08:21.720
after floor of a skyscraper to bring down
a powerful crime lord.

00:08:22.160 --> 00:08:26.300
The violence here is surprisingly beautiful,
with slow motion and vivid colors used to

00:08:26.300 --> 00:08:27.200
incredible effect.

00:08:27.680 --> 00:08:31.500
If graceful, gory violence is your thing,
then Dredd is required viewing.

00:08:32.240 --> 00:08:37.339
Often described as Avengers 2.5, Civil War
featured tons of Avengers, and told a politically

00:08:37.339 --> 00:08:42.089
charged story that set Earth's Mightiest Heroes
against one another in an eye-popping big-screen

00:08:42.089 --> 00:08:43.080
battle royale.

00:08:43.560 --> 00:08:48.040
Along with giving fans high-stakes heroes
vs. heroes battles, Civil War also introduced

00:08:48.050 --> 00:08:53.220
Black Panther to mainstream audiences and
took a major step toward moving the MCU forward

00:08:53.220 --> 00:08:55.880
by picking over some of the fallout from Age
of Ultron.

00:08:56.180 --> 00:08:59.860
But even if you're not up on all the Marvel
lore, it's still one heck of a fun thrill

00:08:59.860 --> 00:09:00.360
ride.

00:09:00.800 --> 00:09:05.639
More explosive, more affecting, and funnier
than the first, Guardians of the Galaxy Vol.

00:09:05.639 --> 00:09:10.930
2 is another snarky space epic powered by
a soulful classic rock soundtrack and awesome

00:09:10.930 --> 00:09:11.420
visuals.

00:09:11.740 --> 00:09:15.800
This time around, the Guardians square off
against Ayesha, high priestess of The Sovereign,

00:09:15.800 --> 00:09:17.680
and eventually the godlike Ego.

00:09:18.100 --> 00:09:22.880
Memorable performances from Pom Klementieff,
Karen Gillan, Michael Rooker, Sylvester Stallone

00:09:22.880 --> 00:09:25.920
and Kurt Russell also make this sequel a must-see.

00:09:26.300 --> 00:09:30.880
Critics who quibbled with Vol. 2's hyperactive
style and emotional moments missed one of

00:09:30.880 --> 00:09:33.040
the funniest movies in Marvel's collection.

00:09:33.500 --> 00:09:38.740
Until 2017, Thor was little more than a pompous
prince who liked hitting things with a hammer

00:09:38.740 --> 00:09:40.720
and took himself way too seriously.

00:09:41.020 --> 00:09:45.600
Marvel just needed the right filmmaker to
turn this Asgardian into a likable guy, and

00:09:45.610 --> 00:09:49.880
they found it with Taika Waititi, who scaled
back the Shakespearean theatrics and turned

00:09:49.880 --> 00:09:51.660
Thor into a well-meaning goofball.

00:09:51.940 --> 00:09:53.480
"I choose to run toward my problems.

00:09:53.480 --> 00:09:55.240
And not away from them."

00:10:00.860 --> 00:10:05.880
Paired with a nebbishy Bruce Banner, Ragnarok
becomes an Odd Couple comedy in space, and

00:10:05.880 --> 00:10:07.480
the funniest film in the MCU.

00:10:07.800 --> 00:10:12.920
Add an '80s aesthetic, the super-cool score,
Thor battling Hulk in a gladiator match, and

00:10:12.931 --> 00:10:17.041
a cast that includes Jeff Goldblum at his
strangest, and all the problems out of the

00:10:17.041 --> 00:10:19.320
Thor franchise are perfectly hammered out.

00:10:19.900 --> 00:10:24.340
The Winter Soldier is much more than just
a superhero movie, it's Marvel getting political.

00:10:24.780 --> 00:10:28.940
Winter Soldier finds a recently-thawed Steve
Rogers in a world where things aren't quite

00:10:28.960 --> 00:10:30.060
black and white anymore.

00:10:30.460 --> 00:10:34.680
It's hard to know who to trust, and Cap quickly
finds himself in the middle of a conspiracy

00:10:34.840 --> 00:10:39.940
that involves secret Hydra agents, metal-armed
assassins, and, worst of all, an evil Robert

00:10:39.940 --> 00:10:40.440
Redford.

00:10:41.120 --> 00:10:43.880
With the fate of the world hanging in the
balance, Cap goes rogue.

00:10:44.340 --> 00:10:48.820
Winter Soldier features some of the most suspenseful
scenes you'll ever see in a superhero film,

00:10:48.820 --> 00:10:52.180
with tense moments that boil over into fantastic
action scenes.

00:10:52.320 --> 00:10:55.920
The film also shakes up the MCU, setting up
the stakes for Civil War.

00:10:56.540 --> 00:11:00.800
Winter Soldier is a masterclass in action
and tension, and the best entry in the Captain

00:11:00.800 --> 00:11:01.900
America franchise.

00:11:02.640 --> 00:11:07.040
Though the big-screen Superman is dark and
dreary these days, he got his start as a brilliant

00:11:07.040 --> 00:11:08.520
red-and-blue beacon of hope.

00:11:08.860 --> 00:11:15.160
Richard Donner's 1978 Superman starring Christopher
Reeve was an instant classic, pulling in an

00:11:15.300 --> 00:11:19.380
A-list cast and telling a classic story complete
with a dastardly Lex Luthor.

00:11:19.720 --> 00:11:24.540
From the cutting-edge special effects to the
casting of then-unknown Reeve as Clark Kent,

00:11:24.800 --> 00:11:28.959
Superman set the template for the modern-day
superhero movies, proving you could take these

00:11:28.960 --> 00:11:32.180
characters seriously and still have a whole
lot of fun in the process.

00:11:32.820 --> 00:11:37.560
M. Night Shyamalan's Unbreakable was a brilliant
exploration and deconstruction of comic book

00:11:37.570 --> 00:11:41.720
characters at a time when superhero movies
weren't the juggernauts of Hollywood they'd

00:11:41.720 --> 00:11:46.260
soon become, and a radical departure from
the superhero films that had come before.

00:11:46.420 --> 00:11:50.760
Unbreakable treated superheroes seriously,
laying the groundwork for many comic book

00:11:50.760 --> 00:11:51.640
movies to come.

00:11:52.040 --> 00:11:57.590
Plus, the movie is just good; Bruce Willis
and Samuel L. Jackson give outstanding performances,

00:11:57.590 --> 00:12:01.920
the score is incredibly haunting, and the
film created a universe where James McAvoy

00:12:01.920 --> 00:12:04.020
would someday unleash his inner beast.

00:12:04.580 --> 00:12:08.420
Change was overdue in the MCU when Black Panther
pounced onto the scene.

00:12:08.860 --> 00:12:12.960
Played by Chadwick Boseman, T'Challa first
showed up in Civil War and quickly became

00:12:12.960 --> 00:12:13.800
a fan favorite.

00:12:14.280 --> 00:12:19.750
The courageous cat made his triumphant return
in 2018, and when his film hit theaters, audiences

00:12:19.750 --> 00:12:21.180
fell in love with Wakanda.

00:12:21.500 --> 00:12:22.660
"This never gets old."

00:12:30.420 --> 00:12:34.500
Black Panther is one of the highest-grossing
films of all time, and the first superhero

00:12:34.520 --> 00:12:36.900
movie to get an Oscar nomination for Best
Picture.

00:12:37.420 --> 00:12:42.460
Talented actors like Lupita Nyong'o, Daniel
Kaluuya, and Angela Bassett struck a chord

00:12:42.470 --> 00:12:47.600
with audiences, and the African setting allowed
filmmaker Ryan Coogler to explore a rich culture

00:12:47.600 --> 00:12:49.840
that's little-seen in Hollywood films.

00:12:50.280 --> 00:12:55.720
The film also introduced one of the greatest
bad guys in superhero history: Erik Killmonger.

00:12:55.920 --> 00:13:00.500
Played to villainous perfection by Michael
B. Jordan, Killmonger is a stone-cold, but

00:13:00.500 --> 00:13:01.660
sympathetic, murderer.

00:13:02.110 --> 00:13:06.280
With its fantastic characters and beautiful
world-building, it's no wonder Black Panther

00:13:06.280 --> 00:13:07.380
was a breakthrough hit.

00:13:08.040 --> 00:13:12.660
The superhero movie genre is mostly dominated
by dudes, but the gender roles were finally

00:13:12.660 --> 00:13:17.940
reversed in 2017 when the most iconic female
hero finally got her own movie.

00:13:18.260 --> 00:13:23.620
Wonder Woman was a critical success and a
box office smash, reinvigorating DC's superhero

00:13:23.620 --> 00:13:26.780
universe and giving kids a different kind
of hero to look up to.

00:13:27.140 --> 00:13:32.420
In a DC franchise that had up until then been
defined by grit and gloom, this Amazon princess

00:13:32.420 --> 00:13:34.800
emerged as a beacon of courage and hope.

00:13:35.320 --> 00:13:38.190
She isn't punching down cities or branding
bad guys.

00:13:38.190 --> 00:13:41.160
She's a protector of the people trying to
end all war.

00:13:41.640 --> 00:13:46.839
Unlike the DCEU's Batman or Superman, Diana
actually cares about people and sees the good

00:13:46.840 --> 00:13:47.620
in humanity.

00:13:48.020 --> 00:13:51.020
She's more concerned with saving lives than
serving justice.

00:13:51.180 --> 00:13:55.170
Superman's symbol might stand for "hope,"
but it's Wonder Woman that restored our faith

00:13:55.170 --> 00:13:57.280
in the power of superheroes.

00:13:57.800 --> 00:14:02.079
Spider-Man: Into the Spider-Verse takes the
iconic wall-crawler's web-slinging mythos

00:14:02.079 --> 00:14:07.420
in exciting new directions by introducing
audiences to a vibrant world of parallel dimensions,

00:14:07.420 --> 00:14:09.900
parallel lives, and talking cartoon pigs.

00:14:09.900 --> 00:14:12.220
"You got a problem with cartoons?"

00:14:14.640 --> 00:14:20.600
The plot follows teenage Miles Morales who's
bitten by, you guessed it, a radioactive spider.

00:14:20.880 --> 00:14:25.440
But things get even more complicated when
a powerful machine opens up portals to other

00:14:25.440 --> 00:14:30.370
worlds, blasting a whole team's worth of alternate
universe Spider-People into Miles' New York

00:14:30.370 --> 00:14:30.860
City.

00:14:31.200 --> 00:14:35.160
The film's brilliant animation captures the
feeling of reading the comic book like few

00:14:35.160 --> 00:14:36.400
movies have before it.

00:14:36.800 --> 00:14:41.600
It couples the visuals with a daring story
that takes a daunting multiverse concept and

00:14:41.600 --> 00:14:45.540
roots it in character moments that any viewer
can relate to, young or old.

00:14:45.950 --> 00:14:50.520
Most superhero movies are about special people
doing the impossible, Into the Spider-Verse

00:14:50.520 --> 00:14:54.240
is a rare gem that makes you feel like you
can do the impossible too.

00:14:54.700 --> 00:15:00.160
2017's Logan finally allowed Hugh Jackman's
Wolverine the R-rated chance to slice and

00:15:00.160 --> 00:15:02.680
dice his foes like Marvel's own Freddy Kreuger.

00:15:03.060 --> 00:15:06.660
But the movie is so much more than just an
extra-bloody X-Men adventure.

00:15:07.080 --> 00:15:11.960
It's an ode to a hero at the end of his life,
and a somber meditation on violence, regret,

00:15:11.960 --> 00:15:12.620
and redemption.

00:15:13.100 --> 00:15:18.380
Inspired by classic Westerns and the Old Man
Logan comic books, Logan stands apart from

00:15:18.380 --> 00:15:20.060
the rest of the X-Men series.

00:15:20.410 --> 00:15:24.860
It takes the nearly-unkillable Wolverine and
brings him back down to earth as a broken,

00:15:24.880 --> 00:15:26.200
forlorn mortal man.

00:15:26.580 --> 00:15:30.940
Jackman and co-star Patrick Stewart give some
of the best performances of their careers

00:15:30.960 --> 00:15:35.160
with stark portrayals of their characters
as dying men in a defeated world.

00:15:35.620 --> 00:15:39.939
Their last mission is to protect Laura, a
young clone of Wolverine's who still has hope

00:15:39.940 --> 00:15:40.720
for the future.

00:15:41.060 --> 00:15:46.060
The three leads' surprisingly familial connection
makes for a grounded and emotional story that

00:15:46.069 --> 00:15:49.370
resonates in a way few superhero movies can
match.

00:15:49.370 --> 00:15:52.240
"Bad s--- happens to people I care about.

00:15:52.520 --> 00:15:53.420
Do you understand me?"

00:15:56.240 --> 00:15:57.300
"Then I'll be fine."

00:15:58.100 --> 00:16:02.540
2004's The Incredibles is still one of the
best superhero movies, and one of the best

00:16:02.540 --> 00:16:03.620
Pixar movies too.

00:16:04.210 --> 00:16:08.120
It's full of brilliant little moments that
stick in your memory, like the hilarious interviews

00:16:08.140 --> 00:16:11.300
that open the film, or the macabre "no capes"
montage.

00:16:11.600 --> 00:16:16.240
There's also the fact that this is a kids'
movie that deals seriously with adult themes;

00:16:16.240 --> 00:16:20.170
characters go through midlife crises, and
grapple with hiding their identities in a

00:16:20.170 --> 00:16:21.620
world that won't accept them.

00:16:22.209 --> 00:16:26.240
The action sequences are fluid and fun, just
as thrilling as almost anything you'll see

00:16:26.240 --> 00:16:28.640
in a live-action Marvel or DC film.

00:16:28.960 --> 00:16:32.850
But what really elevates the movie is the
family at the center of the story, who are

00:16:32.850 --> 00:16:35.020
charming both at home and on the battlefield.

00:16:35.440 --> 00:16:37.880
They're also completely believable as a family
unit.

00:16:38.260 --> 00:16:42.740
"Both of you will get a grip or so help me
I will ground you for a month.

00:16:42.740 --> 00:16:43.740
Understand?!"

00:16:44.480 --> 00:16:50.480
After 11 years and 21 films, the Marvel Cinematic
Universe brought the Infinity Saga to a close

00:16:50.480 --> 00:16:56.130
with Endgame, an epic action flick that smashed
box office records and said farewell to some

00:16:56.130 --> 00:16:58.180
of our most beloved superheroes.

00:16:58.440 --> 00:17:03.420
Despite running three hours long, it never
feels its length, with each act feeling wildly

00:17:03.420 --> 00:17:04.660
different from the last.

00:17:05.020 --> 00:17:09.880
It all leads up to the most ambitious superhero
battle ever filmed, featuring dozens of characters

00:17:09.880 --> 00:17:13.880
from across the MCU in a climactic battle
for the fate of the universe.

00:17:14.520 --> 00:17:19.080
Though it starts off with a tone of mourning,
Endgame ends up feeling like an absolute joy.

00:17:19.520 --> 00:17:24.300
Its biggest achievement is that it truly works
as the finale to a decade-plus of storytelling.

00:17:24.600 --> 00:17:29.560
Watching all of Marvel's characters reunite
one last time is stirring, and while the MCU

00:17:29.570 --> 00:17:34.260
will likely continue long past the original
six Avengers, Endgame provides the perfect

00:17:34.260 --> 00:17:36.060
conclusion to their story as a team.

00:17:36.740 --> 00:17:42.040
The granddaddy of the MCU, Iron Man is just
as good today as it was in 2008.

00:17:42.240 --> 00:17:47.100
With heavy hitters like the X-Men and Spider-Man
already sold off to larger studios, Marvel

00:17:47.100 --> 00:17:50.520
had to pull heroes from the bench to launch
its shared universe.

00:17:50.920 --> 00:17:55.100
Iron Man was one of the best of the rest,
so director Jon Favreau was given a lot of

00:17:55.100 --> 00:17:58.360
freedom, and the studio banked on the charisma
of Robert Downey, Jr.

00:17:58.860 --> 00:18:03.360
The gamble worked, and this movie managed
to tell an extremely fun story while setting

00:18:03.360 --> 00:18:07.000
the tone for a massive $20 billion franchise
to follow.

00:18:07.200 --> 00:18:11.800
It's also a textbook example of how to get
a superhero origin story right.

00:18:12.540 --> 00:18:13.460
"I am Iron Man."

00:18:17.560 --> 00:18:21.920
Over the course of ten years and 18 films,
Marvel had been preparing for the most ambitious

00:18:21.920 --> 00:18:26.460
crossover event in movie history, and when
it came time for the world's mightiest heroes

00:18:26.460 --> 00:18:31.180
to fight the universe's biggest bad guy, the
results were better than anyone could've dreamed.

00:18:31.700 --> 00:18:37.080
2018's Infinity War quickly became one of
the highest-grossing films of all time, integrating

00:18:37.080 --> 00:18:39.320
countless characters into a cohesive world.

00:18:39.800 --> 00:18:44.400
Most importantly, Infinity War totally delivered
when it came to the Mad Titan, who Marvel

00:18:44.400 --> 00:18:47.220
fans had been eagerly awaiting since 2012.

00:18:47.640 --> 00:18:51.840
In a surprising twist, Marvel even made Thanos
the film's true protagonist.

00:18:52.360 --> 00:18:57.340
And then, the Mad Titan wins the day in one
of the gutsiest endings in blockbuster history.

00:18:57.560 --> 00:19:02.660
Watching so many beloved characters turn to
dust is absolutely heartbreaking, but it also

00:19:02.660 --> 00:19:07.140
set the stage for the climactic finale to
Hollywood's most successful franchise.

00:19:07.780 --> 00:19:10.020
"I am Groot!"

00:19:11.000 --> 00:19:12.000
"I am Steve Rogers!"

00:19:12.360 --> 00:19:17.180
The pinnacle of the MCU was established relatively
early on, with the first ever team-up of Earth's

00:19:17.180 --> 00:19:21.680
Mightiest Heroes in The Avengers, written
and directed by fan favorite Joss Whedon.

00:19:22.180 --> 00:19:25.500
The result proved an unqualified critical
and commercial hit.

00:19:25.700 --> 00:19:27.440
"A new universe!"

00:19:27.720 --> 00:19:33.440
It's one of the most successful films ever
made, pulling in more than $1.5 billion worldwide,

00:19:33.560 --> 00:19:37.420
and it scored some of the best reviews earned
by any of the year's wide releases.

00:19:37.660 --> 00:19:42.040
It's a comic book brought to life in the best
possible way, and Whedon managed to blend

00:19:42.040 --> 00:19:47.000
a bevy of characters, geek-out fan service,
and a compelling story into one perfect package.

00:19:47.700 --> 00:19:53.120
The superhero movie genre was in its infancy
in 2004, but despite being practically ancient,

00:19:53.120 --> 00:19:55.160
Spider-Man 2 still holds up.

00:19:55.360 --> 00:20:00.480
This is a movie that features an Evil Dead-style
horror sequence, a superhero showdown on a

00:20:00.490 --> 00:20:04.330
train, the most heartbreaking date ever filmed,
and a villain who feels like an old-timey

00:20:04.330 --> 00:20:05.520
Universal monster.

00:20:05.800 --> 00:20:08.420
None of this should fit together, but it all
works perfectly.

00:20:08.880 --> 00:20:09.880
"Spider-Man!

00:20:09.880 --> 00:20:10.880
Spider-Man!

00:20:10.880 --> 00:20:14.360
Does whatever a spider can!

00:20:14.740 --> 00:20:17.300
Spins a web, any size…"

00:20:17.600 --> 00:20:22.160
But Spider-Man 2 really shines by giving us
the most relatable superhero of all time.

00:20:22.340 --> 00:20:28.260
Unlike the mega-rich Batman or the nearly-immortal
mutant Wolverine, Peter is just a normal guy,

00:20:28.270 --> 00:20:31.900
trying to deliver pizza and woo the girl of
his dreams while keeping the streets of New

00:20:31.900 --> 00:20:32.880
York safe.

00:20:33.400 --> 00:20:37.040
When he's not fighting supervillains, he's
struggling with everyday problems.

00:20:37.170 --> 00:20:41.400
Yeah, he can shoot webs and climb walls, but
this version of the wall-crawler is still

00:20:41.400 --> 00:20:43.840
the most human superhero we've ever seen.

00:20:44.220 --> 00:20:49.020
The Dark Knight isn't just the best superhero
movie ever made; it ushered in a new era for

00:20:49.020 --> 00:20:50.260
comic book movies.

00:20:50.570 --> 00:20:55.260
Suddenly, superhero movies could be high art,
worthy of awards and accolades, all thanks

00:20:55.260 --> 00:20:58.100
to the Caped Crusader and the Clown Prince
of Crime.

00:20:58.280 --> 00:21:01.900
Here was a film with one of the greatest opening
sequences of all time.

00:21:02.020 --> 00:21:06.380
It explored heavy concepts like what people
will do when forced into terrible circumstances,

00:21:06.380 --> 00:21:10.100
and told the tragic story of the rise and
fall of Harvey Dent.

00:21:10.540 --> 00:21:14.020
It also featured the greatest 18-wheeler flip
of all time.

00:21:14.660 --> 00:21:19.380
Heath Ledger won a posthumous Oscar for his
turn as the chaos-loving Joker, and all these

00:21:19.380 --> 00:21:23.680
years later, people still shudder when they
remember his freaky scars and his terrifying

00:21:23.680 --> 00:21:24.440
magic trick.

00:21:24.960 --> 00:21:29.880
It's a performance for the ages, and thanks
to Ledger, the Joker joined the best cinematic

00:21:29.880 --> 00:21:32.340
villains, alongside Darth Vader and Hannibal
Lecter.

00:21:32.840 --> 00:21:37.120
With its impressive acting, pounding score,
impeccable direction, and intense action,

00:21:37.120 --> 00:21:41.540
The Dark Knight is the kind of superhero movie
that fans deserve and need.

00:21:43.100 --> 00:21:44.280
"I'm just ahead of the curve."

